    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nAll-New 2028 Mazda BT-50 Is Less a Workhorse and More a Lifestyle Pickup Truck in Fresh Renderings\n6 photos\nPhoto: kolesaru / Instagram\nThe Japanese automaker Mazda , one of the smaller ones but also one of the most beloved, is constantly looking toward the horizon – and currently they’re focused on both EVs like the Mazda 6e or CX-6e as well as lightweight sports cars like the MX-5 Miata, which is potentially going to stay light and analog plus ICE-powered.\nMazda this year focused on the introduction of the latest CX-5 compact crossover SUV to its most important regions, as well as bringing the new CX-6e alongside the Mazda 6e in places like the Old Continent. But their future plans not only include the very light Miata sports car but, as it turns out, also a heavy workhorse, the Mazda BT-50 pickup truck.\nIntroduced two decades ago in 2006 as a sibling of the Ford Ranger and a successor to the B-Series pickups, the Mazda BT-50 is not produced or sold in its home market because its main location is in Thailand. Currently in its third generation, the model continues to share its underpinnings with another model, this time around the Isuzu D-Max since 2020, and received a facelift in 2024.\nAlas, Mazda is already contemplating the future of the BT-50, and the rumor mill firmly believes it has a future and a fourth iteration is brewing. Just like all the other generations, the new one will share its underpinnings with an existing model since Mazda can’t develop the model alone, and while we’re waiting for confirmation on the donor model, the speculation concerns either the next-gen Isuzu D-Max or a switch to a Changan model, as Mazda already collaborates with the Chinese automaker on the Mazda 6e and CX-6e.\nNaturally, the rumor mill isn’t idle, either, and has asked a member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators to stop dwelling across the parallel universes of vehicular CGI to envision the next generation of the Mazda BT-50. More precisely, the good folks at Kolesa , along with their resident pixel master Nikita Chuicko, aka ' kelsonik ' on social media, have imagined the next-gen truck based on the Chinese Changan Hunter pickup truck.\nHowever, the pixel master has used Mazda’s current design language to showcase the new model, although there is no information yet about the exterior design of the upcoming truck. So, take it with a pinch of salt, but this unofficial, hypothetical design project features the signature U-shaped LED backlit grille outline, has split headlights tucked above the bumper with integrated LED fog lights, and a host of protections at the front and rear, along with side steps.\nAt the back, there’s an integrated bumper with a diffuser and a step, along with vertical LED taillights and a full-width LED bar plus an integrated spoiler into the tailgate. All in all, this is now akin to a lifestyle model rather than a workhorse, right? View this post on Instagram A post shared by Колёса.ру (@kolesaru)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2028 Mazda BT-50 Mazda BT-50 Mazda BT-50 CGI new generation rendering kelsonik kolesa\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Six EVs Burn Down in Cadillac Dealership Inferno Amid GM Battery Recall",
